<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <Description>The shared in-memory model for wind and wave grids read from GRIB2 and NetCDF-CF files: a regular latitude/longitude weather grid set, the canonical parameter table with its GRIB2 and CF mappings, normalisation to the coverage pipeline's grid order, and an ICoverageSource with lazily decoded time steps, overview levels, wind speed and direction derived from U and V, and code-defined coverage styles for wave height, wind barbs, wind speed and wave direction. Also the surface analysis model (fronts, troughs and pressure centres) and a reader for the WPC coded surface bulletins, standard, high resolution and forecast. And the storm-ink portrayal of a tropical cyclone advisory: its cone, wind radii, tracks and WMO class symbols. Not for navigation. Depends on EncDotNet.S100.Core, EncDotNet.S100.Portrayals and EncDotNet.S100.Datasets.TropicalCyclones.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="EncDotNet.S100.Datasets.Weather.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\EncDotNet.S100.Core\EncDotNet.S100.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\EncDotNet.S100.Portrayals\EncDotNet.S100.Portrayals.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\EncDotNet.S100.Datasets.TropicalCyclones\EncDotNet.S100.Datasets.TropicalCyclones.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The wind barb, calm and wave arrow symbols, served by WeatherCoverageStyle.Symbols.
         Generated by tools/GenerateWeatherSymbols. -->
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Symbols\*.svg" LogicalName="EncDotNet.S100.Datasets.Weather.Symbols.%(Filename)%(Extension)" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
